#: includes/class-admin.php:171
msgid "Suggested text: This plugin needs a large language model to turn a plain-English question into a database query. Nothing is sent until an administrator asks a question or uses the connection test. Which AI service receives the request depends on the Backend setting under WooCommerce &rarr; Siphon Store Analytics &rarr; Settings:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:173
msgid "WordPress AI Client (the default): the request is sent by WordPress itself to the provider connected under Settings &rarr; Connectors. This plugin stores no API key on this path, and the terms and privacy policy of whichever connector is active apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:174
msgid "Your own API key: the request goes directly to the endpoint entered in Settings (OpenAI, Claude/Anthropic, OpenRouter, DeepSeek, Groq, Mistral, xAI, or a custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint), with that key sent as an authorization header so the provider can bill your account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:176
msgid "On each request the following is sent over HTTPS to the AI service:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:178
msgid "Your question, in plain text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:179
msgid "Database schema metadata only: table names and column names."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:180
msgid "The model, temperature, reasoning effort and token limit selected in Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:182
msgid "No customer, order, product, or payment records are transmitted. Generated queries run against this site's own database and their results are never sent to the AI service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:184
msgid "The connection test in Settings sends only a short fixed prompt (Say \"ok\" and nothing else.) to the same service. Through the WordPress AI Client that service is whichever provider is connected under Settings &rarr; Connectors. With your own key it depends on the endpoint entered in Settings: by default OpenAI, Claude (Anthropic), OpenRouter, DeepSeek, Groq, Mistral or xAI. A self-hosted endpoint such as Ollama, LocalAI or vLLM keeps the data inside your own infrastructure. Terms of service and privacy policy links for each provider are listed in the plugin readme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:186
msgid "Locally, the plugin keeps the question, the generated query and its display settings so past insights can be re-run; it does not keep the result rows. A generated answer is cached for the duration configured under Cache Duration so the same question does not call the AI twice. All of this data is removed when the plugin is deleted. Password hashes, activation keys and session tokens are never included in the schema sent to the provider and cannot be queried."
msgstr ""

